    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (81.17) and **Trea Turner** (79.76). **Yordan Alvarez** remains the premier play against Yesavage, benefiting from a superb 0.448 xwOBA and a favorable platoon advantage that drives his efficiency toward the elite tier. Meanwhile, **Trea Turner** exploits the softest matchup of the day against Palmquist; with a 6.00 xERA opposing him and a 100% stolen base opportunity against the pitcher\u2019s delivery, **Trea Turner** is a lock for multi-category production. **Christian Yelich** also earns a strong recommendation (74.33) as he faces Lowder in a setup that maximizes his platoon edge, positioning him to lead the offensive effort alongside our top-tier performers.\n\nThe depth of the roster forces some difficult tactical calls, specifically regarding our bench. **Lars Nootbaar** (43.39) served as the primary bubble candidate, ultimately pushed out by the higher efficiency scores of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (60.02) and **Carson Benge** (61.40). While **Lars Nootbaar** maintains a respectable floor, his negative platoon split against Bratt suppressed his ceiling compared to the speed-oriented profiles of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Carson Benge**, both of whom are prioritized for their elite stolen base potential. We remain cautious regarding **Casey Schmitt**, whose 45.53 score is contingent on a pending lineup slot; if he drops out of the three-hole, his value will dip further. Additionally, keep an eye on **Pete Crow-Armstrong** against McLean; while his platoon advantage is strong, the threat of an elite catcher behind the plate (1.87s pop time) introduces a slight drag on his SB probability, requiring active monitoring throughout the game.",
